description.narrative:
The oPt Emergency Appeal.
The oPt EA defines the following three strategic priorities for UNRWA humanitarian response in oPt:
SP 1: increased economic access to food for crisis-affected Palestine refugees;
SP 2: maintaining access to critical services;
SP 3: effective coordination and management of the emergency response.

UNRWA Flash Appeal: 90 day initial emergency response to the escalation in the Gaza Strip
UNRWA aims to provide multi-sectorial support, and its flash appeal is in coordination with OCHA's Flash appeal. UNRWA's response consists of a few key prioritized response activities (1) provision of support in emergency shelters, including food and water provision, NFI:s, repairs of shelters, primary health care provision etc. (2) emergency health support to hospitals (3) multi-purpose cash assistance.

The Syria, Lebanon and Jordan Emergency Appeal
The EA defines the following three strategic priorities for UNRWAs humanitarian response:
SP 1: ensuring the most vulnerable Palestine refugees meet their basic needs;
SP 2: maintaining access to basic services;
SP 3: improving the effectiveness and efficiency of emergency programme delivery.
